# L §2.1, §2.5 (tally 2.1.7 R10, issue #149; #113a): a four-digit literal where a period is expected is a year
# through parentheses and in an if's branches: day_of((2026), 12-31), end_of((2026)), end_of(if ...), (if ...) +
# 1 year; a step in parentheses takes its operand's unit. 2.1.6's refcore refused `day_of is 2 026, not a period`.
# (T's carried p_day_of.)
=== model.tally
model years
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
  note "T's carried items 5 and 6 (issue #108, invented): a parenthesised literal is that literal wherever the bare one stands (L §2.1, the coordinator's picks P6 and P12), and #97's N1, the written year forms; each form is a file of its own beside this base"

source card "T's card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index ys = year 2026..2027

index ms = month 2026-01..2027-12

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

input rate[y in ys]: num

input start_day: date

input wage[m in ms]: money PLN

ask base: rate[2026], rate[2027], year_of(start_day) == 2026, day_of(2026, 12-31), wage[2026-06], wage[2027-06], bal(konto, 2026-01-05)

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  rate[2026] = 0.1 "the card"
  rate[2027] = 0.2 "the card"
  start_day = 2026-01-05 "the card"
  wage = 5000.00 PLN governs 2026 "the card"
  wage = 5200.00 PLN governs 2027 "the card"
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "the card"
=== y_paren.tally
part y_paren
  tally 2

ask p_day_of: day_of((2026), 12-31)

ask y_end: end_of((2026))

ask y_end_if: end_of(if year_of(start_day) == 2026 then 2026 else 2027)

ask y_plus_if: (if year_of(start_day) == 2026 then 2026 else 2027) + 1 year

ask y_round: round(wage[2026-06], (1), down)
=== expect p_day_of y_end y_end_if y_plus_if y_round
p_day_of: 2026-12-31
  cut 2026-10-01
y_end: 2027-01-01
  cut 2026-10-01
y_end_if: 2027-01-01
  cut 2026-10-01
y_plus_if: 2027
  cut 2026-10-01
y_round: 5 000.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-01
